0,5,inf
0
```

Note node 3: the direct edge costs 8, but going 0-2-3 costs 2, which is what the relaxation finds.

**Approach**

The time for a signal to reach every node is the maximum of the shortest path distances from the source. So run Dijkstra and take the largest finite distance, reporting failure if any node is unreachable.

**Logic**

Dijkstra settles nodes in order of distance using a min-heap. Since .NET's PriorityQueue has no decrease-key, push improved distances as new entries and skip stale pops using a settled flag.

The answer is the maximum over all nodes, not the sum, because the signal propagates in parallel: every node receives it at its own shortest-path time, and the network is fully covered when the last one does.

O((V + E) log V).

**Program**

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution
{
    // times[i] = [from, to, weight], nodes numbered 1..n
    public static int NetworkDelayTime(int[][] times, int n, int source)
    {
        var graph = new List<(int To, int Weight)>[n + 1];
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) graph[i] = new List<(int, int)>();
        foreach (var t in times) graph[t[0]].Add((t[1], t[2]));

        var dist = new int[n + 1];
        Array.Fill(dist, int.MaxValue);
        dist[source] = 0;

        var settled = new bool[n + 1];
        var heap = new PriorityQueue<int, int>();
        heap.Enqueue(source, 0);

        while (heap.Count > 0)
        {
            int node = heap.Dequeue();
            if (settled[node]) continue;      // a stale duplicate entry
            settled[node] = true;

            foreach (var (next, weight) in graph[node])
            {
                int candidate = dist[node] + weight;
                if (candidate < dist[next])
                {
                    dist[next] = candidate;
                    heap.Enqueue(next, candidate);
                }
            }
        }

        // The network is covered when the LAST node receives the signal.
        int slowest = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
        {
            if (dist[i] == int.MaxValue) return -1;   // unreachable
            slowest = Math.Max(slowest, dist[i]);
        }

        return slowest;
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(NetworkDelayTime(new[] {
            new[] { 2, 1, 1 }, new[] { 2, 3, 1 }, new[] { 3, 4, 1 } }, 4, 2));

        Console.WriteLine(NetworkDelayTime(new[] { new[] { 1, 2, 1 } }, 2, 1));
        Console.WriteLine(NetworkDelayTime(new[] { new[] { 1, 2, 1 } }, 2, 2));   // 1 unreachable
        Console.WriteLine(NetworkDelayTime(Array.Empty<int[]>(), 1, 1));          // single node
        Console.WriteLine(NetworkDelayTime(new[] {
            new[] { 1, 2, 1 }, new[] { 1, 3, 4 }, new[] { 2, 3, 1 } }, 3, 1));    // 1-2-3 beats 1-3
    }
}
```

