**Approach**

The natural framing — which balloon to burst first — fails, because bursting changes the neighbours of everything else, so subproblems overlap in a way that cannot be decomposed.

Invert it: decide which balloon is burst **last** within a range. That balloon's neighbours are then fixed, being the boundaries of the range, so the left and right parts become independent subproblems.

**Logic**

Pad the array with a 1 at each end so every balloon has neighbours. `best[i][j]` is the most coins obtainable from bursting everything strictly between i and j.

For each `k` in that open range, if k is burst last, it earns `nums[i] * nums[k] * nums[j]` because i and j are still standing by definition, plus the best of the two independent halves.

Iterate by increasing range width so the halves are always already computed. O(n³) time, O(n²) space.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution
{
    public static int MaxCoins(int[] nums)
    {
        if (nums == null || nums.Length == 0) return 0;

        int n = nums.Length;

        // Pad with 1s so every balloon has a neighbour.
        var padded = new int[n + 2];
        padded[0] = padded[n + 1] = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) padded[i + 1] = nums[i];

        var best = new int[n + 2, n + 2];

        // Widening ranges, so the two halves are always solved first.
        for (int width = 2; width <= n + 1; width++)
            for (int left = 0; left + width <= n + 1; left++)
            {
                int right = left + width;

                for (int last = left + 1; last < right; last++)
                {
                    // 'last' burst last: its neighbours are still left and right.
                    int coins = padded[left] * padded[last] * padded[right]
                              + best[left, last] + best[last, right];

                    best[left, right] = Math.Max(best[left, right], coins);
                }
            }

        return best[0, n + 1];
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(MaxCoins(new[] { 3, 1, 5, 8 }));
        Console.WriteLine(MaxCoins(new[] { 1, 5 }));
        Console.WriteLine(MaxCoins(new[] { 5 }));
        Console.WriteLine(MaxCoins(new int[0]));
        Console.WriteLine(MaxCoins(new[] { 1, 1, 1 }));
        Console.WriteLine(MaxCoins(new[] { 9, 76, 64, 21 }));
    }
}
```

