What   must   be|acknowledgment  |shall be        
single    
a b|c  
```

**Approach**

Two pointers from both ends. Advance each until it lands on a vowel, swap, and continue inward.

**Logic**

Non-vowels stay exactly where they are, so the pointers skip them. Only when both point at vowels does a swap occur.

The detail worth getting right is case: both upper and lower case vowels count, and the case travels with the letter rather than with the position, so swapping characters directly gives the correct result.

O(n) time, O(n) space only because C# strings are immutable and a char array is needed.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution
{
    private const string Vowels = "aeiouAEIOU";

    public static string ReverseVowels(string s)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)) return s;

        var chars = s.ToCharArray();
        int left = 0, right = chars.Length - 1;

        while (left < right)
        {
            while (left < right && Vowels.IndexOf(chars[left]) < 0) left++;
            while (left < right && Vowels.IndexOf(chars[right]) < 0) right--;

            if (left < right)
            {
                (chars[left], chars[right]) = (chars[right], chars[left]);
                left++;
                right--;
            }
        }

        return new string(chars);
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(ReverseVowels("hello"));
        Console.WriteLine(ReverseVowels("leetcode"));
        Console.WriteLine(ReverseVowels("aA"));          // case travels with the letter
        Console.WriteLine(ReverseVowels("bcd"));         // no vowels
        Console.WriteLine(ReverseVowels(""));
        Console.WriteLine(ReverseVowels("Programming"));
    }
}
```

