```
holle
leotcede
Aa
bcd

Prigrammong
```

**Approach**

A word qualifies only if every prefix of it is also in the dictionary. Sort so that shorter words come first, then build up a set of qualifying words, checking each candidate against its own prefix.

**Logic**

Sorting by length ensures that when a word is examined, every shorter word has already been considered, so checking whether `word[..^1]` is in the buildable set is sufficient — the rest of the chain was verified transitively.

Single-character words have an empty prefix, which counts as buildable, so they seed the set.

Ties are broken lexicographically, so sorting by length then alphabetically means the first qualifying word of maximal length is the answer and no comparison is needed afterwards.

O(n log n) for the sort, then linear.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public class Solution
{
    public static string LongestWord(string[] words)
    {
        if (words == null || words.Length == 0) return "";

        // Shortest first, then alphabetical, so the first qualifying longest wins.
        var sorted = words.OrderBy(w => w.Length).ThenBy(w => w, StringComparer.Ordinal);

        var buildable = new HashSet<string> { "" };   // the empty prefix seeds it
        string best = "";

        foreach (string word in sorted)
        {
            // Only the immediate prefix needs checking: the rest was verified already.
            if (!buildable.Contains(word[..^1])) continue;

            buildable.Add(word);
            if (word.Length > best.Length) best = word;
        }

        return best;
    }

    private static string Show(string s) => s.Length == 0 ? "(none)" : s;

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(Show(LongestWord(new[] { "w", "wo", "wor", "worl", "world" })));
        Console.WriteLine(Show(LongestWord(new[] { "a", "banana", "app", "appl", "ap", "apply", "apple" })));
        Console.WriteLine(Show(LongestWord(new[] { "abc", "bc", "ab", "qwe" })));   // no chain
        Console.WriteLine(Show(LongestWord(new[] { "a" })));
        Console.WriteLine(Show(LongestWord(Array.Empty<string>())));
        Console.WriteLine(Show(LongestWord(new[] { "b", "br", "bre", "brea", "break", "a", "ap" })));
    }
}
```

