**Approach**

Walk each diagonal in turn, alternating direction. Cells on the same diagonal share `row + col`, so the traversal is grouped by that sum.

**Logic**

For diagonal d, the cells are those where row + col equals d. Going up-right the row decreases; going down-left it increases. The direction flips on each diagonal.

The bounds are the fiddly part: for diagonal d the row ranges from `max(0, d - cols + 1)` to `min(d, rows - 1)`. Reversing the collected cells on alternate diagonals is simpler than deriving the start point for each direction, and costs nothing measurable.

O(rows × cols) time.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution
{
    public static int[] FindDiagonalOrder(int[][] matrix)
    {
        if (matrix == null || matrix.Length == 0) return Array.Empty<int>();

        int rows = matrix.Length, cols = matrix[0].Length;
        var result = new List<int>(rows * cols);
        var diagonal = new List<int>();

        // Cells on one diagonal share row + col.
        for (int d = 0; d <= rows + cols - 2; d++)
        {
            diagonal.Clear();

            int startRow = Math.Max(0, d - cols + 1);
            int endRow = Math.Min(d, rows - 1);

            for (int r = startRow; r <= endRow; r++) diagonal.Add(matrix[r][d - r]);

            // Even diagonals run up-right, which is the reverse of collection order.
            if (d % 2 == 0) diagonal.Reverse();

            result.AddRange(diagonal);
        }

        return result.ToArray();
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", FindDiagonalOrder(new[] {
            new[] { 1, 2, 3 }, new[] { 4, 5, 6 }, new[] { 7, 8, 9 } })));

        Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", FindDiagonalOrder(new[] {
            new[] { 1, 2 }, new[] { 3, 4 } })));

        Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", FindDiagonalOrder(new[] { new[] { 1, 2, 3, 4 } })));
        Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", FindDiagonalOrder(new[] {
            new[] { 1 }, new[] { 2 }, new[] { 3 } })));
        Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", FindDiagonalOrder(new[] { new[] { 7 } })));
    }
}
