-10
3
-1
0
```

**Approach**

Bottom-up DP computing the *minimum health required on entering* each cell. Working forwards does not work, and understanding why is the point of the problem.

**Logic**

A forward DP tracking accumulated health fails because the best path so far is not necessarily the best overall: a route that collects more health may pass through a cell that kills you, and the maximum-health path is not the same as the survivable path. The two objectives conflict.

Working backwards fixes it. The requirement on entering a cell is whatever the next cell needs, minus this cell's value, floored at 1 — since health must never drop to zero.

O(rows × cols) time and space.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution
{
    public static int CalculateMinimumHp(int[][] dungeon)
    {
        if (dungeon == null || dungeon.Length == 0) return 1;

        int rows = dungeon.Length, cols = dungeon[0].Length;

        // need[r][c] = health required ON ENTERING that cell.
        var need = new int[rows + 1, cols + 1];

        for (int r = 0; r <= rows; r++)
            for (int c = 0; c <= cols; c++)
                need[r, c] = int.MaxValue;

        // Past the exit, 1 point of health suffices.
        need[rows, cols - 1] = need[rows - 1, cols] = 1;

        for (int r = rows - 1; r >= 0; r--)
            for (int c = cols - 1; c >= 0; c--)
            {
                int onward = Math.Min(need[r + 1, c], need[r, c + 1]);

                // Never allow the requirement to fall below 1.
                need[r, c] = Math.Max(1, onward - dungeon[r][c]);
            }

        return need[0, 0];
    }

    private static int[][] Grid(params int[][] rows) => rows;

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(CalculateMinimumHp(Grid(
            new[] { -2, -3, 3 }, new[] { -5, -10, 1 }, new[] { 10, 30, -5 })));

        Console.WriteLine(CalculateMinimumHp(Grid(new[] { 0 })));
        Console.WriteLine(CalculateMinimumHp(Grid(new[] { -5 })));
        Console.WriteLine(CalculateMinimumHp(Grid(new[] { 100 })));      // still needs 1
        Console.WriteLine(CalculateMinimumHp(Grid(new[] { 1, -3, 3 }, new[] { 0, -2, 0 },
                                                 new[] { -3, -3, -3 })));
    }
}
