**Approach**

Expand around every centre. There are 2n-1 centres — n characters for odd-length palindromes and n-1 gaps for even-length ones — and each expansion counts every palindrome it finds.

**Logic**

From each centre, expand outward while the characters match, incrementing the count on every successful step. Each distinct substring is counted exactly once because a palindrome has exactly one centre.

The common failure is checking only odd centres, which misses every even-length palindrome and would report 3 rather than 4 for "aaa".

O(n²) time, O(1) space. Manacher's gives O(n) but is rarely expected.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution
{
    public static int CountSubstrings(string s)
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)) return 0;

        int count = 0;

        for (int centre = 0; centre < s.Length; centre++)
        {
            count += ExpandFrom(s, centre, centre);       // odd length
            count += ExpandFrom(s, centre, centre + 1);   // even length
        }

        return count;
    }

    private static int ExpandFrom(string s, int left, int right)
    {
        int found = 0;

        while (left >= 0 && right < s.Length && s[left] == s[right])
        {
            found++;        // every successful expansion IS a palindrome
            left--;
            right++;
        }

        return found;
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(CountSubstrings("abc"));     // three single characters
        Console.WriteLine(CountSubstrings("aaa"));     // a,a,a,aa,aa,aaa
        Console.WriteLine(CountSubstrings(""));
        Console.WriteLine(CountSubstrings("a"));
        Console.WriteLine(CountSubstrings("abba"));
        Console.WriteLine(CountSubstrings("aaaa"));
    }
}
```

**Output**

```
