**Approach**

Two-dimensional DP over prefix lengths. `can[i][j]` is true when the first i characters of s1 and the first j of s2 can interleave into the first i+j of s3.

**Logic**

Greedy matching fails: when the next character of s3 matches both s1 and s2, taking either one may be the only path that works, and you cannot tell which without looking ahead. The DP explores both.

A state is reachable if it can be entered by consuming one more character from s1, or one more from s2, with that character matching s3 at the combined position.

The length check is the cheap early exit and also guards the indexing.

O(m × n) time, reducible to O(n) space with a rolling row.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution
{
    public static bool IsInterleave(string s1, string s2, string s3)
    {
        s1 ??= ""; s2 ??= ""; s3 ??= "";

        if (s1.Length + s2.Length != s3.Length) return false;

        // row[j] = can the first i of s1 and first j of s2 make the first i+j of s3?
        var row = new bool[s2.Length + 1];
        row[0] = true;

        for (int j = 1; j <= s2.Length; j++)
            row[j] = row[j - 1] && s2[j - 1] == s3[j - 1];

        for (int i = 1; i <= s1.Length; i++)
        {
            row[0] = row[0] && s1[i - 1] == s3[i - 1];

            for (int j = 1; j <= s2.Length; j++)
            {
                bool fromS1 = row[j] && s1[i - 1] == s3[i + j - 1];       // row[j] is still i-1
                bool fromS2 = row[j - 1] && s2[j - 1] == s3[i + j - 1];    // row[j-1] is already i

                row[j] = fromS1 || fromS2;
            }
        }

        return row[s2.Length];
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("aabcc", "dbbca", "aadbbcbcac"));
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("aabcc", "dbbca", "aadbbbaccc"));
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("", "", ""));
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("", "b", "b"));
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("a", "b", "ab"));
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("a", "b", "ba"));
        Console.WriteLine(IsInterleave("abc", "de", "abcd"));   // wrong total length
    }
}
```

