13
```

**Approach**

Single pass with a length check first. If the lengths differ by more than one the answer is immediately false; otherwise walk both strings and allow exactly one divergence.

**Logic**

Normalising so the shorter string is first removes the symmetric cases. Then there are only two situations at the first mismatch: equal lengths means a replacement, so skip one character in each; different lengths means an insertion, so skip one character in the longer only.

After the divergence the remainders must match exactly, which the loop enforces by continuing without allowing a second difference.

O(n) time, O(1) space.

**Program**

```csharp
using System;

public class Solution
{
    public static bool IsOneEditDistance(string a, string b)
    {
        a ??= ""; b ??= "";

        if (a.Length > b.Length) (a, b) = (b, a);   // normalise: a is the shorter

        if (b.Length - a.Length > 1) return false;
        if (a.Length == b.Length && a == b) return false;   // identical is zero edits

        int i = 0, j = 0;
        bool used = false;

        while (i < a.Length && j < b.Length)
        {
            if (a[i] == b[j]) { i++; j++; continue; }

            if (used) return false;
            used = true;

            // Equal lengths: a replacement. Different: an insertion into the longer.
            if (a.Length == b.Length) i++;
            j++;
        }

        return true;   // any leftover is at most the single trailing insertion
    }

    public static void Main()
    {
